# .trivyignore — the media service's scanner exception register (D-23,
# POL-06 seed; Plan 03-07, Task 3).
#
# Empty today — no exception exists yet because none has been needed.
# This file's SHAPE matters more than its current emptiness: it is the
# seed of Phase 7's estate-wide exception register, and every future
# entry here MUST follow the discipline
# scripts/check-trivyignore.sh enforces (run as a workflow step, so an
# unjustified entry fails the run, not merely a style nit a reviewer might
# miss):
#
#   # Reason: <finding id/description> — <why this is accepted, and by
#   #   whom/until when if relevant>
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#
# The comment line(s) directly above a finding ID are that finding's
# justification — check-trivyignore.sh requires a real, non-empty,
# non-boilerplate reason immediately preceding every entry. A bare
# `CVE-YYYY-NNNNN` with no preceding comment, or a comment reading only
# "todo"/"n/a"/similar, fails the lint exactly like an un-justified
# `checkov:skip=` fails scripts/verify-checkov-skips.sh in athena-infra —
# the same discipline, applied to this estate's second scanner.
#
# MUST NOT be used to silence a finding in order to turn a red gate green
# (this plan's own prohibition, restated at the point where it would be
# easiest to violate): every entry here is a deliberate, reviewable,
# justified acceptance of a specific, named risk — never a way to route
# around the gate.
